==English==

===Etymology===
From Latin ''[[advocatus diaboli]]'', "devil’s advocate"

===Noun===
{{en-noun|sg=[[devil]]’s [[advocate]]}}

# {{idiomatic}} One who [[debate]]s from a view which they may not actually hold, usually to determine its [[validity]], or simply for the sake of [[argument]].
# (''Roman Catholic Church'') A [[canon]] lawyer appointed by the [[Church]] to argue against the canonization of the proposed [[candidate]].
{{wikipedia}}

